      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "[International Business Identifier (IBID)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the [ISO/DIS 25500-3](https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html) draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (`|`) (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420`)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "ibid"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvidenceType",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "EvidenceType refers to categories of documented or observable proof used to verify compliance, qualification, or performance"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/probability",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A probability score between 0 and 1 of a vulnerability being exploited."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/assumptionStatement",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A text describing the design constraint defined by the assumption."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isci",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "International Standard Collection Identifier (ISCI) is a variable-length identifier standardized by [ISO 27730](https://www.iso.org/standard/44293.html) for identifying collections held by libraries, archives, museums, and other memory institutions. It consists of two parts: the identifier for the assigning organization (an ISIL) enclosed in square brackets, followed by a local collection identifier string (e.g., `[FR-751041001]Casadesus1`)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "isci"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "[International Standard Content Code (ISCC)](https://iscc.io/) is a content-derived identifier standardized by [ISO 24138](https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html) for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like `ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI`."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "iscc"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/VexJustificationType/componentNotPresent",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/VexJustificationType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The software is not affected because the vulnerable component is not in the product."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "componentNotPresent"
